-- title:
--   Per-node conclusion at the K₀-traces of all ends
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and a finite set $W$ of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field of $A$, together with an element $s$ of $W$. Assume the inclusion `hle` of the base-changed level-$M'$ modular function field into `fieldBar q M'`, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$, i.e. a valuation subring of the upper field together with a surjective residue map onto the characteristic-$p$ function field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue map, and a degree- and order-preserving map on places. Further data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with elements $\pi_0$ (lying in $A$), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$; a natural number $\ell$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ that is exactly the preimage of $A$, and $\varpi_b\in A_b$; a prime $\ell'$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$, an algebra over $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) in a scalar tower with $k_0$; a non-zero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$; $\varpi_t'\in A_0$; an ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, the algebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t\subseteq W_t$; a natural number $n$; $\gamma_0\in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$; a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; a natural number $m$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal; the hypothesis that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$ lies in $K_\ell$; $a_0\in A_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. All of these are assumed to satisfy the bundled hypotheses $\mathcal F$ of the structure `RigidDescentHyps`. Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(K_\ell/k_0)$ generated by those $\tau$ for which there is $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ with `IsLevelAutAt` holding for $k_0$, the root of unity datum $\xi$ of order $q\ell'$, level $((q\ell')^2M',\ \mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')$, the matrix $\gamma^{-1}$ and $\tau$ — that is, $\tau$ transforms every quotient of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of that level in the way prescribed by the weight-$k$ slash action of $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$, under any embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ consist of the elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$, let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by $W_t$, and let `nodes` be a finite set of subrings of $K_0$ each of which is the trace on $K_0$ of some member of `ends`. The conclusion is that for every $\tilde{\mathcal O}\in$ `ends` and every subring $\mathcal O$ of $K_0$ equal to the preimage of $\tilde{\mathcal O}$ under $K_0\hookrightarrow K_\ell$, the predicate `PernodeConclusion` holds for all the above data together with $G$, $K_0$, $B_0$, $W_0'$, `nodes` and $\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the per-node block of the descent of the rigid supersingular chart of the modular curve to the field $K_0$ fixed by the level automorphisms: every end of the rigid model has its trace on $K_0$ satisfying the required local description at a node. It feeds the statement assembling the descended model, its common chart, nodes, Igusa branch and separation data over the fixed field.
